# Domains that commonly return 403/429 to automated checkers (bot protection)
# even when the link is fine for a real browser. Excluded to avoid false alarms.
facebook\.com
instagram\.com
linkedin\.com
# Google Maps "search" deep links are generated, not pages that 404; skip them.
google\.com/maps
maps\.google\.com
# The card renderer in index.html builds markup by string concatenation, e.g.
#   '<a href="' + esc(l.href) + '"' ...     '<img ... src="' + img + '"/>'
# lychee --include-verbatim reads the raw source and treats those JS fragments
# as href/src values, reporting them as phantom file:// "not found" errors.
# It opened a fresh issue on every run. These are code, not links.
# Patterns match the URL as lychee reports it (space -> %20).
esc\(l\.href\)
%20\+%20img%20\+%20
# The card renderer in index.html builds markup by string concatenation, e.g.
#   '<a href="' + esc(l.href) + '"' ...     '<img ... src="' + img + '"/>'
# lychee --include-verbatim reads the raw source and treats those JS fragments
# as href/src values, reporting them as phantom file:// "not found" errors.
# It opened a fresh issue on every run (60 so far). These are code, not links.
# Patterns match the URL as lychee reports it (space -> %20).
esc\(l\.href\)
%20\+%20img%20\+%20
